  "result": "The gate returned **OK** for `NRS_484B_307_5a_o2` (9 witnesses), on the 4th of 6 allowed runs.\n\n**What I wrote:**\n- **Who it applies to:** a road user in both the \"traffic\" and \"vehicle\" groups that faces signal head `s`. Facing means it is on an approach lane that `s` controls and that enters intersection `i`, or it entered `i` from such a lane and has stayed in it since. The rule applies while `s` shows the green straight-through arrow and no other light. If the head reports a lamp the source couldn't read, \"arrow alone\" is left unknown, not decided.\n- **The duty:** it covers every other vehicle or pedestrian that is in `i` or in a crosswalk at one of `i`'s entrances. That person must be there now, and must also have been there when the arrow last came on alone. The subject must not move faster than the halt tolerance while heading into a near-collision with them (closest approach within 3 s and closer than 3 m), and must not touch them.\n- **Witnesses:** the five planned scenes, plus four more so that every part of the formula affects at least one outcome:\n  - a car that enters the intersection and closes on a stalled car;\n  - a car that stays stopped while another car passes close by;\n  - the arrow shown together with a round green light;\n  - the arrow becoming the only light one step after it first appears.\n\n**Gate runs:**\n1. On the untouched files before I edited, which used up a run.\n2. Accidental: I piped the gate into another command and its output was thrown away.\n3. Failed on the `blind` scene. The verdict was unknown for the wrong reason: Core treats \"does this region enter intersection `i`?\" as unknown when the region is the intersection itself. I fixed it by excluding `i` from the approach-lane checks. The definitions of approach lanes say an intersection never is one, so no real approach is lost.\n4. OK.\n\nI also tried to run the gate with `--help` to see its options. That was blocked by the permission settings, so I didn't use it.\n\n**For the harness:** Core gives \"which intersection does this region enter?\" as unknown for any region without a lane record, including intersections, where false would be correct. Other rules that loop over all travel regions will hit the same problem.\n\nThe report is in `task_result.md` in the working directory.",
